# Copy to `config.env` at the REPO ROOT and fill in. Every module resolves this one file from
# __file__, so it loads no matter which directory you run from.
#
#   cp config.env.example config.env
#
# `config.env` is gitignored. This example file is not — keep real keys/paths out of it.
#
# Renamed from api.env 2026-07-28: this file grew beyond API keys once the Unity-sim filesystem
# paths below stopped being hardcoded per-developer absolutes (C:\Sari\..., a specific person's
# C:\Users\<name>\... — each broke on every machine but the one it was written on) and became
# settings instead. "config.env" reflects that it now covers all machine-specific configuration,
# not just credentials.

# --- Agent runtime: UCL vLLM server (Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B) ---------------------------
# Required for anything that drives the agent. Retired OpenRouter for agent calls
# (2026-07-19 user directive) when its credits ran out.
# OPENAI_API_URL is a BARE HOST — the code appends :8000/v1 itself. No scheme, no port.
# The server 401s without a bearer key (measured 2026-07-19).
OPENAI_API_URL=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Unity sim: filesystem -------------------------------------------------------
# The Unity project is a SEPARATE repo (see overhaul/CLAUDE.md) - there is no path to it that
# works across machines, so it is not guessed or hardcoded. overhaul/sim/sim_paths.py reads these.
#
# Root of the Unity sim repo — the folder that contains Assets/Resources/Data/*.json (Categories.json,
# PriceData.json). Used by the completion guard's catalog grounding (orchestrator/subtask_completion.py)
# and the offline scoring/reconciliation scripts (slamtest/scoring/*.py). Grounding degrades gracefully
# to plain substring matching when unset; the scoring scripts require it and fail loudly without it.
# SARI_SANDBOX_DIR=/path/to/SariSandboxV2

# The Unity save file the sim writes at runtime (shelf placements ground truth for score_index.py's
# per-slot scoring). Typically under Unity's persistentDataPath, e.g. on Windows:
#   C:\Users\<you>\AppData\LocalLow\Sari Sandbox\Sari Sandbox V2\Store 2 v2.json
# SARI_STORE_SAVE_JSON=/path/to/Store 2 v2.json

# --- Unity sim: network ------------------------------------------------------------
# The sim's WebSocket command server. overhaul/sim/env.py reads this (resolved per call, so
# subtask_agents' --ws-uri can override it at runtime); md_tools.py and the slamtest scripts still
# carry their own hardcoded defaults. Distributed Sari Bench sets it per attempt to the sandbox it
# leased, which is how several agents run against different sims at once.
# SARI_WS_URI=ws://localhost:8080/commands

# --- Central OCR service ----------------------------------------------------------
# Every agent sends in-memory PNG receipt crops to one runner-local PaddleOCR daemon. Start it with
# `uv run poe ocr-server`. Flags named --ocr-url take precedence over this variable; the final
# default is http://127.0.0.1:9100. Agents never construct a local Paddle model or fall back locally.
# SARI_OCR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9100

# --- Third-party -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Moondream cloud API — the agent runtime's only non-self-hosted dependency.
# Used by md_tools.py and perception.py.
MDREAM_API_KEY=

# Gemini — legacy root stack (functions.py, comprehension.py).
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — LEGACY. Credits exhausted (402); agent calls moved to the UCL server.
# Still read by agent.py's OpenRouterConfig default and subagent_run.py.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Replicate — no reader found anywhere in the codebase. Present in the original
# api.env; safe to drop unless something outside this repo uses it.
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=

# --- Legacy root stack -----------------------------------------------------------
# The LitServe inference server that run.py posts to. Hardcoded at run.py:10 today.
# SARI_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:8005/predict

# Legacy fallback for OPENAI_API_URL/OPENAI_API_KEY when neither is set above: agent.py and
# annotate_probe.py read a conda-meta state file for machines that invoke sari_env_old's
# python.exe directly (skips the activation hooks that normally set these vars). Only needed if
# you rely on that setup; the hardcoded default is a specific Windows conda install and will not
# exist on most machines, which is fine — it's a last-resort fallback, not a requirement.
# SARI_CONDA_STATE=C:/Sari/sari_env_old/conda-meta/state
